			"Message": "feat(Sky): Wire status bar and command bridges into workbench services\n\nReplaces the no-op status bar handlers from the previous commit with real integrations using the workbench services exposed via `__CEL_SERVICES__`. Extension-contributed status bar items from `vscode.window.createStatusBarItem(...)` now route through `IStatusbarService.addEntry()`, enabling them to render in the same `.statusbar` DOM as stock VS Code items.\n\nAdds a new command bridge layer that bridges Cocoon → workbench command invocations:\n- `sky://command/execute` calls `ICommandService.executeCommand` and resolves the result back to the extension\n- `sky://command/register` registers extension commands into `CommandsRegistry`, with invocation fan-out back to Cocoon via `ResolveUIRequest`\n- `sky://command/unregister` disposes the registration\n\nThe status bar set-message handler now only dispatches DOM CustomEvents for Sky-side observers rather than dual-routing, as the workbench handles ephemeral messages through its own path.\n\nThis completes the status bar integration that was previously deferred and enables extension commands to execute against the workbench.",
			"SHA": "ea2932ae02487b23967cbab690a7991ec1d19001"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Auto",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T02:21:58Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				81,
				1
			],
			"Message": "",
			"SHA": "d120bcd0a892d275e30a85b1a3fc234117a71d92"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T01:21:59Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				81,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Sky): Remove fallback status bar bridge and add SCM event bridge\n\nDrops the custom fallback status bar that was overlaying VS Code's native `.statusbar`. Extension-contributed status bar items are now dropped until `MainThreadStatusBar.$setEntry` is properly wired into the workbench's `IStatusbarService`. This restores the native status bar appearance.\n\nAdds SCM event bridge handlers that dispatch `cel:scm:*` CustomEvents when Mountain emits `sky://scm/{register,unregister,updateGroup}`. This gives Sky-side components a consumer for SCM state events that would otherwise report \"0 listeners\" drops in the cel-dispatch logs.\n\nRemoves: StripCodicons, GetOrCreateStatusBarItem, EnsureFallbackStatusBar. Status bar handlers become no-ops.",
			"SHA": "05efccae90bfa7b81f00ff14a2936f0643165066"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T00:08:14Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				81,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Sky): Strip codicon syntax from status bar text and isolate fallback bar\n\nThe bridge now removes VS Code codicon syntax (`$(name)`, `$(name~spin)`) from status bar text before rendering. Stock workbench substitutes these for codicon font glyphs; the bridge doesn't parse them, so raw `$(sync~spin)` + Unicode placeholder codepoints were rendering as garbled \"weird emojis\" in the fallback bar.\n\nAlso changes status bar items to ALWAYS use the dedicated fallback bar - never inject into VS Code's native `.statusbar`. Mixing extension-routed items with native workbench DOM mixes two rendering systems and produced the \"not the default status bar\" appearance. Bridge items now live in a separate bar that workbench doesn't manage, so the two coexist without visual conflict.\n\nApplies StripCodicons to both create and update handlers.",
			"SHA": "2ed0e226517e9f005354fb79f674b124a114ea63"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T22:53:29Z",
